// SharesColorWith(ref): a Predicate matching objects that share a color with
// `ref` [CR#702.13b] — the candidate-relative predicate Intimidate needs, built
// on the general It/Where bridge. The matched candidate is `It`, so
// "shares a color with ref" is "for some color, both It and ref are that
// color", over the five colors [CR#105.1]. `ref` is a bare Reference, e.g.
// SharesColorWith(This). The 5-branch is INLINED, not a reuse of a SharesColor
// condition macro: a macro body can't pass its own Param as an argument to a
// nested macro invocation (the nested macro expands before the param binds), so
// composition isn't available here — the set-theoretic ColorsOf/Intersect form
// (which would compose) waits on a color-set value language.
(
    name: "SharesColorWith",
    kinds: [Predicate],
    params: [Reference],
    body: Where(Or([
        And([Matches(It, ColorIs(White)), Matches(Param(0), ColorIs(White))]),
        And([Matches(It, ColorIs(Blue)), Matches(Param(0), ColorIs(Blue))]),
        And([Matches(It, ColorIs(Black)), Matches(Param(0), ColorIs(Black))]),
        And([Matches(It, ColorIs(Red)), Matches(Param(0), ColorIs(Red))]),
        And([Matches(It, ColorIs(Green)), Matches(Param(0), ColorIs(Green))]),
    ])),
)
